  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2y$ is enclosed between the line $y=\\sqrt{x}$ and the $x$-axis for $0\\le x\\le 1.$ Find the moment of the plate about the $y$-axis.",
  "worked_solution": "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={\u222c}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068268/assets/ddc11fc93f034c3d650854e21f178716c941c18f12eb94123e1af2c835c47981.png)\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}}\n$$\n\nand $\\lambda (x,y)=2y.$ \n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={\u222c}_{D}x\\cdot 2y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{D}2xy\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2xy\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x}}2y\\,\\text{d}y]\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\cdot [{y}^{2}]_{y=0}^{y=\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(x-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}]}_{x=0}^{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
